    "about": {
      "type": "chapter-about",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "ABOUT THIS CHAPTER",
        "show_warp_icon": true,
        "katha": "Two Telugu-speaking states, two ways of using colour. In Andhra Pradesh, Mangalagiri weavers make crisp cotton with a gold-flecked border. In Telangana, ikkat weavers tie and dye the yarn before it ever touches a loom. Both are practical, beautiful and easy to wear every day.",
        "about": "The South chapter in our house is built around the Telugu states. Mangalagiri, near Vijayawada in Andhra Pradesh, is known for sturdy handloom cotton with a signature border. Ikkat, woven most famously in Pochampally in Telangana, is a resist-dyed technique where patterns are dyed into the yarn first. One cloth is clear and structured, the other soft-edged and graphic, and together they cover nearly everything from a work shirt to a wedding saree.",
        "fact_1_value": "5",
        "fact_1_label": "states",
        "fact_2_value": "Handloom",
        "fact_2_label": "made in small runs",
        "background_color": "#f6f2ea",
        "warp_icon_color": "#b08d57",
        "padding_top": 60,
        "padding_bottom": 60
      }
    },
    "landscape": {
      "type": "chapter-landscape",
      "settings": {
        "heading": "The landscape behind the loom",
        "paragraph_1": "Andhra Pradesh and Telangana sit on the Deccan plateau, with the Krishna and Godavari running through them. Cotton grows well here, and the region has long had both farmers and weavers who understood it.",
        "paragraph_2": "Mangalagiri, in Guntur district, is a temple town on the road to Vijayawada. Its handloom cotton is plain by design: solid colours, fine checks and stripes, set off by a border with small zari motifs.",
        "paragraph_3": "Pochampally, in Telangana, is the best-known centre of ikkat in the region. Weavers there work in village clusters where tying, dyeing and weaving are done by different hands in the same neighbourhood, passing the yarn along from one stage to the next.",
        "image_position_mobile": "below_text",
        "background_color": "#ffffff",
        "padding_top": 60,
        "padding_bottom": 60
      }
    },
